course: dictionary
lesson: 8044
title: Going back: the word regression
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Regression means going back to an earlier, worse or less developed state. When you meet it, look for that idea of something moving backwards. It is a word used in several subjects, and its exact meaning depends on where you find it.
explain: In computing, regression is a bug. «A fix can break something else, called a side effect; re-testing everything that used to work after each fix is called regression testing.» The clue is «used to work»: a regression is when something that worked stops working. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: In maths, a regression line is the line of best fit drawn through the dots on a scatter graph. In psychology, a child who suddenly acts younger than their age, perhaps after a new baby arrives, is showing regression. Read the words around the word first, because they will tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Regression means going back to an earlier, worse or less developed state.
fact: In computing, a regression is a bug where something that used to work stops working.
fact: A regression line is the line of best fit on a scatter graph, showing how one thing changes with another.
fact: In psychology, regression can mean a child starts acting younger than their age, for example after a shock.
fact: The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning fits the subject you are reading about.
exercise: «A fix can break something else, called a side effect; re-testing everything that used to work after each fix is called regression testing.» What does regression testing check for? | *Things that used to work and have stopped working | Which fix was the cheapest | New games for the children to play | How many times the fix was tested in the lab
exercise: A regression line is drawn through the dots on a scatter graph. What is it for? | Colouring in the dots | A line that always stops at zero | Measuring how long the graph is | *Showing the line of best fit, to see how one thing changes with another
exercise: After her baby brother came home, Maya began sucking her thumb and asking for a bottle again. What is this called? | Progress | Expansion | *Regression | Revision
test: Ella's reading slipped back to an earlier level after she was ill. Which word describes this? | *Regression | Promotion | Expansion | Revision
test: Why might a tester run old tests again after a fix? | To find out who wrote the fix | *To check that things which used to work still work | To delete the old tests | To make the tests harder
exam: Tom says regression means getting better every time. Is he right? | Yes, but only in computing | Yes, it always means improving | *No, it means going back to an earlier, worse state | No, it only ever means a line on a graph
